<% content_for :title, "Code of Conduct" %>
<% content_for :description, "The standards everyone at a Bmore on Rails event agrees to, and how to report a problem." %>

<%#
  DRAFT — this text is adapted from widely used community codes of conduct
  (the Citizen Code of Conduct and the Berlin Code of Conduct lineage) and has
  not yet been ratified by the organizers. Two things must be settled before
  launch: the real reporting contacts in app/models/site.rb, and the names of
  the people who make enforcement decisions.
%>

<article class="bg-white">
  <header class="bg-harbor-900 px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-marble-50 sm:text-5xl">
        Code of Conduct
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-harbor-100">
        Bmore on Rails is meant to be one of the friendlier rooms you can walk
        into. This is what we expect from each other, and what happens when
        someone falls short.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          Who this applies to
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Everyone at a Bmore on Rails event: attendees, speakers, sponsors,
          organizers, and volunteers. It covers our in-person meetups, our
          online spaces, and any venue or after-event gathering where we are
          together as this group.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          What we expect
        </h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-3">
          <% [
               ["Be welcoming.", "Assume the person asking a basic question belongs here, because they do. Most of us were that person recently."],
               ["Be considerate.", "People come with different backgrounds, experience levels, jobs, and reasons for being in the room. Talk to them accordingly."],
               ["Be respectful in disagreement.", "Technical arguments are welcome. Contempt, condescension, and point-scoring are not."],
               ["Take responsibility.", "If you hurt someone, listen, apologize plainly, and correct it. Intent doesn't erase impact."],
               ["Look after the space.", "Follow the rules of whatever venue is hosting us, and leave it better than you found it."]
             ].each do |title, body| %>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-gold-400" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
                <strong class="font-semibold text-harbor-900"><%= title %></strong>
                <%= body %>
              </p>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          What is not acceptable
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          The following behavior is unacceptable at any Bmore on Rails event or
          in any of our spaces:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2.5">
          <% [
               "Harassment, intimidation, or discrimination based on gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, disability, neurotype, physical appearance, body size, race, ethnicity, national origin, age, religion, or experience level.",
               "Unwelcome sexual attention, sexual imagery, or sexual language in talks, slides, or conversation.",
               "Deliberate misgendering or use of a name someone no longer goes by.",
               "Threats or incitement of violence, and encouraging any of the above.",
               "Stalking, following, or unwanted photography and recording.",
               "Sustained disruption of talks, discussions, or other events.",
               "Publishing someone's private information without their explicit permission.",
               "Retaliation against anyone who reports a violation of this code."
             ].each do |item| %>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brick-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800"><%= item %></p>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-xl border-2 border-brick-200 bg-brick-50 p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          Reporting a problem
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          If you experience or witness something that breaks this code — or
          anything else that makes you uncomfortable — tell an organizer. At an
          event, organizers will introduce themselves at the start of the night
          and are the people to find. You can also write to us:
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <%= link_to Site::CONDUCT_EMAIL, "mailto:#{Site::CONDUCT_EMAIL}",
                class: "rounded-sm font-display text-lg font-semibold break-all text-brick-700 underline decoration-brick-300 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-brick-900 hover:decoration-brick-700 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-brick-500 sm:text-xl" %>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Reports are handled confidentially. We will not share your name with
          the person you're reporting without your agreement, and we will not
          ask you to repeat the story to a room full of people. You are welcome
          to bring someone with you when you talk to us.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          If you need help contacting venue security or local authorities, or a
          safe way to get home, ask an organizer and we will arrange it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          What happens next
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Organizers will decide on a response based on what happened. Depending
          on severity, that may be a private conversation, a warning, being asked
          to leave an event, or being barred from future events. Organizers may
          act immediately to stop ongoing harm and sort out the details after.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Organizers are held to this code too. A report about an organizer goes
          to the other organizers, and that person takes no part in deciding it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          A note on scope
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          We're a volunteer meetup, not a court. We can control who is welcome in
          our room and our spaces, and we will use that. We can't adjudicate
          things that happen entirely outside the group, though we will take
          seriously any credible concern about someone's safety at our events.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="border-t border-marble-200 pt-6">
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-harbor-600">
          Adapted from the Citizen Code of Conduct and the Berlin Code of
          Conduct, both of which have made community spaces better for years.
          Suggestions and corrections are welcome —
          <%= link_to "open an issue", Site::GITHUB_URL, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener",
                class: "rounded-sm underline decoration-harbor-300 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-harbor-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-harbor-500" %>.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
